{
  "key_findings": {
    "observability_upper_bound": "Closest (most confusable) source-node pair on golden-reference at the canonical hypothesis combo is J1 vs J2, Euclidean distance 108.54 (signature peak magnitudes 61.9 vs 126.1 mg/L -- clearly distinguishable in magnitude, not near-zero). No pair on this network is information-theoretically indistinguishable under full classical-signature evidence, so this network's real model failures cannot be attributed to fundamental unobservability.",
    "oracle_upper_bounds": "Baseline (real pipeline, full-trajectory evidence, N=10): top1=0.9. Oracle classical prior (delta at true source): top1=1.0 (+0.10). Cited full-history-evidence upper bound (temporal-ablation.json, N=20): top1=1.0 (+0.10 vs this script's own baseline). Both oracle substitutions show only modest (~10-point) headroom over an already-high full-trajectory baseline -- meaning, under FULL-TRAJECTORY evidence, neither classical-prior imperfection nor additional history is the dominant bottleneck; this is consistent with (not contradicting) the separately-established finding (temporal-ablation.json) that the dominant real-world gap is EVIDENCE SPARSITY specifically (the LIVE harness's latest-1-snapshot contract), not these oracle-substituted components.",
    "sensor_placement_golden_reference": "On golden-reference (4/4 junctions), layout A (default, 4 sensors) and B (requested 8, clamped to 4) are numerically identical by construction (fused top1=0.5 both). Layout C (sparse, 2 sensors) shows fused top1=0.5 (unchanged from A/B) but classical top1 fell from 0.6 to 0.4 and neural top1 fell from 0.4 to 0.1 -- fusion partially masks a real per-component degradation under sparse coverage even where the final fused metric looks flat (N=10, noisy).",
    "sensor_placement_loop_grid": "NOT a null result on the larger 8-junction network: fused top1 goes 0.3 (sparse, 2 sensors) -> 0.4 (default, 4 sensors) -> 0.6 (full coverage, 8 sensors) -- a real, monotonic, non-trivial sensor-density effect (N=10 per layout, single network/seed family; directional signal, not a precise effect-size estimate)."
  },
